WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.045 --> 00:00:08.146
Nowadays, a new kind of sport is attracting a new breed of players.

2
00:00:08.726 --> 00:00:13.928
These athletes don't belong to a team, they don't wear a uniform, and they often compete against no

3
00:00:13.988 --> 00:00:14.848
one but themselves.

4
00:00:15.568 --> 00:00:18.929
The sports they play are dangerous, crazy, and even death-defying.

5
00:00:19.829 --> 00:00:21.770
Welcome to the world of extreme sports.

6
00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:27.151
Extreme sports have a relatively short history and became popular only in the 1980s.

7
00:00:27.851 --> 00:00:35.768
They include snowboarding, skateboarding, bungee jumping, BASE jumping, indoor climbing, bouldering, and BMX, as well as many more.

8
00:00:36.568 --> 00:00:42.532
These sports are called "extreme" because they often combine speed, height, danger, and difficult stunts.

9
00:00:43.913 --> 00:00:48.115
The rise of extreme sports signals a change in modern attitudes toward sport.

10
00:00:48.816 --> 00:00:54.679
The individual is emphasized rather than the team, and players are bound not by rules, but only by

11
00:00:54.719 --> 00:00:55.640
the limits of safety.

12
00:00:56.340 --> 00:01:01.845
Traditional Western sports, like soccer or hockey, are played in teams with clear sets of rules and regular

13
00:01:01.885 --> 00:01:07.269
matches. Extreme sports, on the other hand, are all about individual effort and accomplishment.

14
00:01:07.990 --> 00:01:12.433
The athletes push themselves to conquer their fears and challenge the limits of skill and daring.

15
00:01:13.154 --> 00:01:17.958
Even though extreme sports involve pushing against limits, safety is always a priority.

16
00:01:18.838 --> 00:01:23.922
Rugby, a type of football, may in fact be more dangerous than many extreme sports because most rugby

17
00:01:23.962 --> 00:01:25.644
players do not wear protective clothing.

18
00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:31.343
In comparison, participants in extreme sports wear pads, helmets, and other protective gear.

19
00:01:32.263 --> 00:01:38.066
Most participants in extreme sports are young men, but women are participating more and more and getting recognized

20
00:01:38.106 --> 00:01:39.507
for their skill and achievements.

21
00:01:40.988 --> 00:01:42.789
Snowboarding is a winter extreme sport.

22
00:01:43.589 --> 00:01:49.713
Snowboarders strap one boot to a wide board and, balancing on their snowboard, slide down snow-covered slopes.

23
00:01:50.593 --> 00:01:52.934
Snowboarding is similar to surfing and skateboarding.

24
00:01:53.575 --> 00:02:00.658
Snowboards were first made in 1977, but only recently have snowboarders been accepted on mountains that until now

25
00:02:00.898 --> 00:02:02.199
have been dedicated to skiing.

26
00:02:02.819 --> 00:02:08.341
Like skiers, snowboarders travel down mountain slopes, but a big part of the sport is also learning and

27
00:02:08.381 --> 00:02:10.382
perfecting jumps, stunts, and tricks.

28
00:02:11.382 --> 00:02:17.165
Snowboarding hills often include jump ramps and a "halfpipe," which is formed by two long, curved ramps that

29
00:02:17.205 --> 00:02:17.805
face each other.

30
00:02:18.646 --> 00:02:23.828
Boarders jump off the ramps and the top edges of the halfpipe, performing tricks while they fly through

31
00:02:23.848 --> 00:02:24.168
the air.

32
00:02:24.756 --> 00:02:30.942
At the 1998 Winter Games in Nagano, Japan, snowboarding was the first extreme sport to become part of

33
00:02:30.982 --> 00:02:31.502
the Olympics.

34
00:02:32.163 --> 00:02:35.445
Competitors jumped into the air as they snowboarded down the halfpipe.

35
00:02:35.926 --> 00:02:40.730
They were judged on how high they flew, how many spins and stunts they did, and their overall

36
00:02:40.770 --> 00:02:45.494
performance. Skateboarding is one of the oldest extreme sports.

37
00:02:46.275 --> 00:02:51.199
It was originally called "sidewalk surfing," and skateboards were first commercially produced in the 1960s.

38
00:02:52.660 --> 00:03:00.046
The first skateboards were very narrow, flimsy, and unstable─if you ran over a pebble, the skateboard would stop!─and

39
00:03:00.186 --> 00:03:01.147
they weren't too popular.

40
00:03:02.028 --> 00:03:07.773
It wasn't until the 1970s that skateboard design evolved and skateboards became wider and easier to ride.

41
00:03:08.513 --> 00:03:13.397
Skateboarding took off among teenagers and young people, and tricks like the "ollie" were invented.

42
00:03:14.198 --> 00:03:18.601
Skateboarders perform an ollie by kicking one end of their board down just as they jump into the

43
00:03:18.741 --> 00:03:24.178
air. The board bounces into the air with the rider, allowing the rider to jump over objects as

44
00:03:24.238 --> 00:03:25.699
he or she rolls along.

45
00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:31.484
Nowadays, "skaters" form a unique subculture with distinctive clothes, music, and hairstyles.

46
00:03:32.865 --> 00:03:37.589
In the extreme sport of bungee jumping, people jump off very high places with a piece of elastic

47
00:03:37.649 --> 00:03:38.790
cord tied to their bodies.

48
00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:43.654
Bungee jumpers fall almost to the ground, stretching the cord until it snaps back.

49
00:03:44.514 --> 00:03:46.096
Then they fly back up through the air.

50
00:03:46.956 --> 00:03:54.506
In the 1950s, filmmaker Richard Attenborough filmed native tribesmen in Vanuatu jumping from tall wooden platforms with vines

51
00:03:54.566 --> 00:03:55.407
tied to their ankles.

52
00:03:56.347 --> 00:04:03.272
This footage inspired an Englishman, Chris Baker, to copy the stunt with elastic, and in 1979 bungee jumping

53
00:04:03.312 --> 00:04:03.793
was born.

54
00:04:04.533 --> 00:04:11.018
Since the mid 1980s, bungee jumpers have leapt off bridges, cliffs, cranes, and tall buildings, including the Eiffel

55
00:04:11.058 --> 00:04:16.061
Tower. In the movie Golden Eye, James Bond bungee jumps off a tall dam.

56
00:04:16.882 --> 00:04:22.933
Over a million bungee jumps have been done worldwide, but falling dizzying heights attached only to an elastic

57
00:04:22.993 --> 00:04:25.494
cord will never be a sport for the faint-hearted!

58
00:04:27.094 --> 00:04:32.716
BASE jumping has perhaps received the most media attention of all extreme sports because of its daring nature

59
00:04:33.796 --> 00:04:36.036
and the not infrequent deaths resulting from it.

60
00:04:37.037 --> 00:04:42.918
BASE jumping is very similar to skydiving, except that BASE jumpers jump off a fixed object like a

61
00:04:42.978 --> 00:04:45.979
bridge or a tall building instead of out of an airplane.

62
00:04:46.919 --> 00:04:50.925
Their parachutes must open quickly and they must land in a very small area.

63
00:04:51.925 --> 00:04:58.207
The vast majority of BASE jumpers are experienced skydivers, but the sport still reports many injuries and deaths

64
00:04:58.407 --> 00:04:58.927
every year.

65
00:05:00.007 --> 00:05:06.129
One difficulty BASE jumpers face is finding places to jump off, because many building owners are reluctant to

66
00:05:06.169 --> 00:05:08.650
give permission for people to parachute off their buildings.

67
00:05:09.610 --> 00:05:16.212
At only one place in the world─the Perrine Memorial Bridge in Idaho─can BASE jumpers jump legally every day

68
00:05:16.252 --> 00:05:16.632
of the year.

69
00:05:17.756 --> 00:05:22.559
On Bridge Day, held once a year at this bridge, over eight hundred BASE jumps are made in

70
00:05:22.599 --> 00:05:23.779
just over six hours!

71
00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:30.003
Rock climbing has become such a popular extreme sport that now you can do it almost anywhere.

72
00:05:31.223 --> 00:05:37.227
You can climb outdoor rock faces, mountains, and cliffs, but you can also climb in the city on

73
00:05:37.287 --> 00:05:39.428
climbing walls in indoor climbing gyms!

74
00:05:40.668 --> 00:05:46.832
A climbing wall is a fake cliff specially designed for indoor climbing, with grips for climber's hands and

75
00:05:46.892 --> 00:05:50.570
feet and special protective mats on the floor at the base of the wall.

76
00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:56.253
Bouldering is a kind of rock climbing in which the athletes climb large boulders or rock faces without

77
00:05:56.293 --> 00:05:56.633
a rope.

78
00:05:57.774 --> 00:06:03.937
In bouldering, figuring out the best climbing route, problem-solving, and technical skills are more important than strength and

79
00:06:03.977 --> 00:06:07.039
endurance because the climb is often short.

80
00:06:08.020 --> 00:06:11.081
But it's usually interesting─just like the boulders themselves!

81
00:06:12.822 --> 00:06:19.441
And, finally, there's the extreme sport of BMX, which involves racing and performing stunts on a kind of

82
00:06:19.481 --> 00:06:21.062
bicycle called "BMX."

83
00:06:22.182 --> 00:06:27.465
BMX is thought to have started in the 1970s when riders modified their bicycles to make them more

84
00:06:27.525 --> 00:06:35.068
exciting. The modified bikes had tougher tires and stronger frames, which allowed riders to race on dirt tracks,

85
00:06:35.848 --> 00:06:38.589
jump in the air, and even balance and spin on their bikes.

86
00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:44.932
BMX racing is popular among younger children and teenagers because all they need to compete is a bike,

87
00:06:45.972 --> 00:06:48.814
some knee and arm pads, and a good bike helmet.

88
00:06:49.975 --> 00:06:56.420
BMX freestyle, in which the riders perform tricks and stunts, will be an official sport at the 2008

89
00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:57.581
Olympics in Beijing.

90
00:06:59.242 --> 00:07:04.026
As more and more people become extreme sports enthusiasts, the way we think of sport is changing.

91
00:07:05.027 --> 00:07:11.272
Players participate in order to test themselves and challenge their physical abilities or to experience a new, exciting

92
00:07:11.332 --> 00:07:18.010
thrill. Some critics argue that corporate marketing has ruined the spirit of extreme sports by turning it into

93
00:07:18.090 --> 00:07:24.873
corporate slogans, such as "live life to the max" (Pepsi) and "just do it" (Nike).

94
00:07:26.094 --> 00:07:34.337
But while extreme sports may be the hot new trend in advertising, the values of extreme sports─practice, perseverance,

95
00:07:34.738 --> 00:07:39.900
risk, safety, and fun─make them just as challenging and thrilling as ever!
